    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "I had no plans on leaving. The only four years that I spent outside of New York were my four years on active duty in the Army, and this has been my home, born and raised. And every time Kathy Hochl says, you know, Donald Trump, we seldom should get on the bus and move to Florida, that only makes me want to stay and fight more. I mean, Hochl is, she's calling on New Yorkers to flee, and she's making the case easier for New Yorkers to leave where you can't blame people for going and not putting New York in timeout, but permanently saying that they're gone. I get it. A lot of folks who used to come visit the state are saying, I'm going to go spend my available weekend or a week in some other state, not going to New York. I get it. But for me, I'm still here. I'm staying on fighting. I have no plans to leave.",
