    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "You are going to freeze deportations? Freeze deportations for the first 100 days. Those who seek come to the United States legally, for example, by making an appointment and coming to a port of entry, a asylum will still be available, still available. But if an individual chooses not to use our legal pathways, if they choose to come without permission and against the law, they'll be restricted from receiving asylum and staying in the United States. This action will help us gain control of our border, restore order into the process. All those people are seeking asylum. They deserve to be heard. That's who we are. We're a nation that says if you want to flee and you're fleeing oppression, you should come. So today, I'm moving past Republican instruction and using the executive authorities available to me as president to do what I can on my own to address the border. This is the first president in the history of the United States of America that's anybody seeking asylum has to do it in another country. That's never happened before in America. We must face the simple truth, to protect America as a land that welcomes immigrants. We must first secure the border and secure it now.",
